# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ISKCON Kakinada — CLIENT env template (Next.js)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or set these as Vercel project env vars.
# NEVER put real secrets in this file — it is committed to git.
#
# Everything here is NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means these values are BAKED INTO THE
# PUBLIC JAVASCRIPT BUNDLE at build time. There is nothing secret in this file
# and nothing here should ever be secret — do not add an API key or token.
#
# Changing any of these requires a REBUILD to take effect. On Vercel: redeploy
# (or restart the build), not just a restart, or the old value stays in the
# bundle.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [REQUIRED] This site's backend base URL, with no trailing slash.
# In production this is the Railway service URL for the Kakinada server. The
# server's CORS allowlist includes the client origin, so a wrong host here
# shows up as failed fetches in the browser console, not as a build error.
# Locally: http://localhost:8080
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
# [REQUIRED] This site's own public origin, with no trailing slash.
# Drives metadataBase, canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, robots.txt, the
# sitemap, and the check-in links in the admin registrations list. It MUST be
# this temple's domain -- pointing it at another site tells search engines
# these pages live elsewhere.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.iskconkakinada.org
# [REQUIRED for Meta Pixel] Facebook Pixel ID. Must EXACTLY match the server's
# META_PIXEL_ID, or Meta rejects the server-side CAPI event as a
# duplicate/mismatch and event dedup silently fails.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
# [REQUIRED for checkout] Razorpay public key. Must match the server's
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID (the "default" account) or the payment modal fails to open.
# This one is designed to be public -- it is the publishable half of the pair.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY=
